      "writtenOn": "2020-06-02T00:43:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I do not know the charge manager or why it is changing the value, just know it is breaking our attach\n\nIt appears to be a mutex race for select_rp() between [Analog Rp: Type-C current level] in charge_manager() and [PD Rp: PD3-Collision Avoidance PD2-BMCFloorClearance] in TCPMv2.\n\n\"Analog Rp\" only applies in implicit contract, until very last bit of PS_RDY-GoodCRC*. (Plus maybe during PR_SWAP from PS_RDY#2-GoodCRC* until PS_RDY#3-GoodCRC*.) \"PD Rp\" applies after that.\n\nCharge_manager() has no concept of there being \"two\" Rp settings.",
      "parentUuid": "611d1e5d_01051e90",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "9f870edbdca30d2e575fadef04cbb1abb625554b",
